    secs but only needs to be done once or whenever you change your xml files.
    
    3) Modify your post script to copy your flat binary file to your run directory with
    the name "postxconfig-NT.txt".  Below is an example:
    
    cp /global/noscrub/Hui-Ya.Chuang/post_trunk_good/parm/postxconfig-NT-NMM.txt ./postxconfig-NT.txt
    
    The reading of flat binary files takes less than a second so you'll see 20~45
    sec run time saving per post run.

